# Luminary marker — cli#477 init banner collapse
- date: 2026-11-06
- branch: fix/init-banner-collapse
- lead: edward-tufte
- supporting: [don-norman, michael-feathers]

## What each lens caught

- edward-tufte (lead) — resolution. The banner was not printing too much ink;
  it was printing the right data at the wrong level of aggregation. One line
  per file is the detail view. A summary surface wants one line per directory.
  Naming it that way found the cause: the grouping key kept the filename, so
  the summary was silently rendering the detail view.
- don-norman — signifier. "44 of 46 hooks" and "11 refused" are the only two
  facts an adopter can act on, and neither named the flag that changes it.
  The refused line now says --force and --verbose.
- michael-feathers — characterization. The two tests that pinned the inventory
  moved to --verbose with their patterns UNCHANGED. A test that gets weakened
  to let a change through stops being a characterization test.
